    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0335" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg223"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 17, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1323.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the subject of the municipal
                    administration of Harbin and in special reference to my No. 1198, of July 3,
                    1909, with which I inclosed a copy of my note of June 23 to the Prince of Ch’ing
                    with regard to municipal organizations on the lands of the Chinese <pb
                        facs="0336" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/> Eastern Railway, I now have the honor
                    to inclose a copy of the reply of the foreign office to the note referred
                    to.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d182-a1.xml" xpointer="d182-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
